                <pb facs="0775" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.001M18/49: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Guggenheim</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-10T15:00:00-05:00">December 10, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>160. President Machado informed the members of his Cabinet that he wanted them to
                    confer and advise him whether in the best interests of Cuba he should resign the
                    Presidency.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Guggenheim</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
